      "description": "Watch Bradford City vs Rochdale highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The Carabao Cup returned to the spotlight on August 8, 2026, as Bradford City hosted Rochdale in an encounter filled with tactical battles and high-stakes intensity. Both sides looked to assert their dominance early in the competition, setting the stage for a compelling night of football. First Half Pressure and the Breakthrough The match began with Rochdale attempting to catch the hosts off guard, as Zain Silcott-Duberry saw an early effort blocked. However, Bradford City soon grew into the game, dictated the tempo, and created several openings through dangerous deliveries from Josh Neufville and Kayden Jackson . Rochdale goalkeeper Nils Ramming was kept busy throughout the opening period, producing fine saves to deny Matthew Pennington and Kayden Jackson as the pressure mounted. The visitors' resistance was finally broken in first-half stoppage time. In the 45th minute (+1), Will Swan demonstrated his clinical edge, pouncing on an opportunity in the centre of the box to fire a right-footed shot into the heart of the goal, giving the Bantams a crucial lead heading into the break. Baldwin Doubles the Advantage In the second half, Rochdale searched for a way back into the contest, with Emmanuel Dieseruvwe threatening from set-pieces, but his headed efforts failed to hit the target. Bradford City remained composed and continued to exploit their superiority in the air. The decisive moment arrived in the 67th minute when Aden Baldwin rose highest to meet a Callum Connolly cross following a corner, heading home from point-blank range to make it 2-0. Closing Stages and Woodwork Denials Despite the two-goal cushion, Bradford City did not sit back. Substitutes Nick Powell and Bobby Pointon injected fresh energy into the attack, with Powell agonisingly hitting the right post in the 76th minute. Ramming continued to be the standout performer for the visitors, making a string of late saves to prevent a heavier scoreline. Rochdale had a late chance through Dajaune Brown , but Jon McCracken stood firm to ensure a clean sheet and a professional victory for the home side."
